I need a haircut.
I always go to the salon in the evening.
I call a salon in Panampilly Nagar.
A receptionist answers the phone.
"Hello, Panampilly Salon," she says.
"Hello, I want an appointment," I say.
"Which day do you want?" the receptionist asks.
"I want it on Wednesday," I reply.
"At what time on Wednesday?" she asks.
I look at my calendar.
"At five-thirty in the evening," I say.
"Okay, booking for Wednesday evening at five-thirty," she says.
"What is your name?" she asks.
"My name is Maya," I say.
"What is your phone number?" she asks.
"Ninety eight, seventy six, fifty four, thirty two, ten," I say.
"Okay Maya, thank you," she says.
"Thank you," I say.
I hang up the phone.
